I have enough information to write my comprehensive review. Let me compile my findings.

**Key verifications completed:**
1. ✅ URIEL+ (arXiv:2409.18472, COLING 2025) — confirmed at ACL Anthology, covers 4,366 languages
2. ✅ CLO (arXiv:2505.14297, ACL 2025) — confirmed DPO-style English-pivot cross-lingual transfer
3. ✅ Qwen3.5-9B — confirmed 248K vocab, 201 languages, no 7B variant; small series is 0.8B/2B/4B/9B
4. ✅ "Less is More" (arXiv:2509.20129, EMNLP 2025) — confirmed at ACL Anthology
5. ✅ TIPA (arXiv:2601.16629, EACL 2026 Findings) — confirmed, correctly described as training-free encoder adapter aggregation
6. ✅ Aya collection — confirmed 513M instances across 114 languages
7. ✅ All Round 2 issues addressed (DPO formulation, URIEL+, curriculum thresholds, DCO, Aya coverage, budget flagging)

**New finding:** Sherkala-Chat (arXiv:2503.01493, March 2025) — trains Llama-3.1-8B for Kazakh using Turkish+Russian+Kazakh data; directly adjacent uncited work.

